<title>ITALY: Ambroveneto board approves capital rise.</title>
<headline>Ambroveneto board approves capital rise.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Banco Ambrosiano Veneto has approved a plan to boost its capital by up to 6.8 trillion lire over five years in preparation for a takeover of 100 percent of the banking assets of savings bank Cariplo.</p>
<p>A statement issued by Ambroveneto said the board had also approved the acquisition of Cariplo's banking interests at a price equivalent to net book value on December 31 1996, minus the book value of Cariplo shareholdings and property holdings, to be spun off ahead of the merger.</p>
<p>The latter would be valued at around 1.7 trillion lire, the statement said.</p>
</text>
